# Harness follow-ups

- Native Claude subagents are launched by Claude Code itself, so no agent-profile field can set their prompt-cache TTL. A `mode: primary` spawn keeps its cache TTL only when Meridian launches it; long-lived native subagents can still rebuild their cache after an idle gap. Needs an upstream Claude Code setting to fix per agent.
- `pi_idle.py`: Revisit the estimated `openai-codex` 1800-second TTL if the backend publishes one or observed cache hits fall. Local data showed 90% hits after 20–30 minute idle gaps.
- `extractors/opencode.py`: Native denials use OpenCode's generic reason and unavailable tools produce no attempted-call event. Reporting Meridian's reason or the missing calls needs an upstream seam or a mediating hook.
- `transcript.py`: Claude compaction setup currently captures the boundary text while the summary lands in the next entry. Once the summary fills the setup slot, narrow the sessions skill's read from two entries to one.

# Remove Cursor (next minor after 0.25)

Cursor is deprecated in 0.25: every launch that resolves to it warns (`harness_deprecated`,
`_CURSOR_DEPRECATION_WARNING` in `launch/context.py`). The next minor release deletes it;
Jimmy approved the removal. Delete:

- Adapter files: `harness/cursor.py`, `connections/cursor_subprocess.py`,
  `projections/project_cursor.py`, `projections/permissions_cursor.py`, `extractors/cursor.py`.
- Order with the `agy` harness work: its first refactor makes the CLI shortcut names and the
  `--harness` help strings come from the registry, the `[harness.<id>]` config keys from
  `HarnessId`, and rewrites `HARNESS_EXTENSION_TOUCHPOINTS`. If it has landed, the removal
  only deletes the registration; skip the edits below to `cli/bootstrap.py`,
  `cli/bootstrap_cmd.py`, `cli/main.py`, `cli/startup/help.py`, `cli/misc_commands.py` and
  `HARNESS_EXTENSION_TOUCHPOINTS`.
- Wiring: `HarnessId.CURSOR` in `core/types.py`; the Cursor imports in
  `harness/__init__.py::_run_bootstrap` and `registry.py::with_defaults`;
  `BASE_COMMAND_CURSOR_SUBPROCESS` and `CURSOR_INACTIVITY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` in
  `launch/constants.py`; `"cursor"` in `cli/bootstrap.py::HARNESS_SHORTCUT_NAMES` and in the
  `--harness` help of `cli/bootstrap_cmd.py`, `cli/main.py`, `cli/startup/help.py` and
  `cli/misc_commands.py`; `_CURSOR_DEPRECATION_WARNING` in `launch/context.py`.
- The Cursor-only inactivity watchdog, which then has no user: `_inactivity_watchdog`,
  `_inactivity_terminal_outcome`, `last_event_at`, `terminated_by_inactivity` and the
  `HarnessId.CURSOR` branch in `launch/streaming_runner.py`; `TriggerKind.INACTIVITY` and
  `inactivity_task` in `launch/streaming/terminal_arbitrator.py`;
  `SUBPROCESS_REPORT_WATCHDOG_POLL_SECONDS` if nothing else uses it.
- Capability flags only Cursor turned off; each becomes a constant, so delete the flag and
  its branch: `accepts_messages` (`adapter.py`; sole read `cli/spawn_message.py::_harness_accepts_messages`,
  whose check becomes unconditional), `supports_primary_launch` (`adapter.py`; the Cursor
  primary refusal in `launch/context.py`, and `launch/resolve.py::validate_harness_compatibility`,
  which has no caller and is only re-exported), `structured_reasoning` on
  `connections/base.py` (written, never read). Shrink `HARNESS_EXTENSION_TOUCHPOINTS` in
  `harness/__init__.py` to match.
- Raise `_MARS_BUNDLE_MIN_VERSION` in `launch/bundle_adapter.py` to the Mars minor that drops
  Cursor, so an older Mars that still routes to it is refused with the upgrade remedy.
- Tests: the inactivity watchdog tests and `test_streaming_attempt_fresh_events_keep_slow_cursor_backend_alive`
  in `tests/integration/launch/test_streaming_runner_watchdog.py`,
  `test_inactivity_terminal_outcome` in `tests/unit/launch/test_streaming_run_conclusion.py`,
  `tests/smoke/spawn-cursor-subprocess.md` (and its row in `tests/smoke/README.md`); rename the
  "Cursor subprocess" failure text in the two `test_streaming_run_conclusion.py` files.
- Docs: `docs/configuration/cursor.md` and its link in `docs/configuration.md`, the Cursor rows
  and sentences in `docs/agent-profiles.md` (harness list, effort table, native config,
  permissions table, spawn-only note, approval notes, child-spawn guardrail), the table row and
  paragraph in `docs/getting-started.md`, `.cursor` in `docs/configuration/mars.md`, `INSTALL.md`,
  `README.md`, `.gitignore`, root `AGENTS.md`, the Cursor sentences in
  `harness/.context/CONTEXT.md`, `projections/.context/CONTEXT.md`, and the two bundled skill
  pages `escalation__meridian/SKILL.md` and `prompt-authoring__meridian/resources/agents.md`.
- Old state must keep reading: make `HarnessId._missing_` raise a clear error for `cursor` ("Cursor
  support was removed in 0.26.0; its sessions can no longer be launched, resumed or read"),
  because about 25 call sites build `HarnessId(value)` and would otherwise say `'cursor' is not a
  valid HarnessId` on `session log`, `--continue` and `--fork` of an old Cursor session. `spawn
  list` and `spawn show` need no change (the record's `harness` is a string). Keep the `cursor`
  chat in `tests/integration/ops/test_legacy_native_import.py` and the `harness_id: "cursor"` line
  in `tests/fixtures/history/wire_envelopes.jsonl`.
- Add an upgrade section for that release, and keep Mars's matching removal in step: a Mars that
  still routes to Cursor then hits `bundle_adapter._parse_harness_id`'s unsupported-routing error.
